{
  "slug": "artist:popcaan",
  "name": "Popcaan",
  "editorial_article": "Born Andrae Hugh Sutherland in Saint Thomas Parish, Jamaica, in 1988, Popcaan rose to prominence in 2008 after joining Vybz Kartel's Gaza Music Empire. His 2010 breakout hit \"Clarks,\" featuring Kartel, triggered a national spike in sales for the British footwear brand. Popcaan transitioned to international acclaim through his 2014 debut album, \"Where We Come From,\" which was executive produced by Dre Skull and released via Mixpak Records. Known for collaborations ranging from Drake to Gorillaz, he has also been featured on Jamie xx’s 2015 track \"I Know There's Gonna Be (Good Times)\" alongside Young Thug. In 2026, he was traditionally honored in Ghana with the chieftaincy title \"Nana Arkoh Kese I\" as Aboafohen of the Apagyahen Division in the Asebu area.",
